  "description": "The Marley Hardtail Frame is a playful and stable frame that's suited to fast singletrack routes, flowing trail sessions and long days in the saddle. Plus, it features a robust and lightweight alloy frame that has a recommended max fork travel of 140mm, clearance for up to 2.6\" tyres and a BSA threaded bottom bracket shell.The Marley has become a classic: light, punchy and versatile. It might be your first bike to explore off-road, or the agile plaything of a seasoned rider. Using 6061 alloy tubing, the Marley balances a stiff frame with enough compliance for the longest of days in the saddle. Geometry is based firmly around fun with a 65.5-degree head angle keeping things stable and confidence inspiring on the rough stuff. Elsewhere on the frame the tick-boxes are checked; ISCG 05 chain guide tabs, a 44/56mm tapered head tube, internal dropper seat post compatibility and 148x12mm boost rear end. Up, down, along and over; the Marley proves a great riding all-rounder doesn’t have to break the bank.",
